  "referenceHtml": "\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-page\" data-elementor-id=\"362\" class=\"elementor elementor-362\" data-elementor-post-type=\"page\">\n\t\t\t\t<div data-particle_enable=\"false\" data-particle-mobile-disabled=\"false\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-88c502c e-con-full e-flex e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"88c502c\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t<div data-particle_enable=\"false\" data-particle-mobile-disabled=\"false\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-df6c749 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"df6c749\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-01d9285 animated-slow elementor-invisible elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"01d9285\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_animation&quot;:&quot;fadeIn&quot;,&quot;_animation_delay&quot;:200}\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Eleanor Herbosch (1999) is a British born, Belgian multidisciplinary artist who manipulates a variety of materials to create textural works of art. In 2019, whilst still studying at London’s Central Saint Martins, she founded her practice in a small studio in the back of her garden in Antwerp, Belgium, where she still resides and works.</p><p> </p><p>Her adopted means of expression are ceramics and painting which are united by a common denominator: earth, her material of choice.</p><p><br>Eleanor’s work is characterised by expressing the potential of natural materials with the intent of enhancing their intrinsic qualities.</p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div data-particle_enable=\"false\" data-particle-mobile-disabled=\"false\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-9cbb9cb e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child\" data-id=\"9cbb9cb\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-t